      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2952431581,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "I am the last one to update it, though I only half-understand how the Lua globals file and test works.\n\nMy understanding is that it holds most of the globals that are defined, and the tests check to make sure that all the globals are present if we claim to support (WS) Lua. However, it also contains a bunch of globals that come straight from Lua, which sometimes are different in different major version of Lua - e.g., I think at some point they stopped providing things like the hyperbolic cosine function from C math. Probably it should be regenerated whenever we add new Lua functions, but it wasn't done for 4.6.\n\nIf it's failing, I would guess that something is missing or has been renumbered.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
